Data Cleaning Transformation in Scala

Aim:- 
To handle missing values in a dataset by replacing them with the mean of the available values.

Program:-
object Main extends App {

  // Dataset: (Name, Marks, Gender)
  // None represents a missing value

  val data = List(
    ("Amit", Some(78.0), "Male"),
    ("Priya", Some(85.0), "Female"),
    ("Rahul", None, "Male"),
    ("Sneha", Some(92.0), "Female"),
    ("Karan", None, "Male"),
    ("Karan", None, "Male"),
    ("Riya", Some(90.0), "Female"),
    ("Sahil", Some(70.6), "Male")
  )

  // Step 1: Handle Missing Values

  println("Original Dataset")
  println("Name\tMarks\tGender")
  data.foreach(println)

  // Step 2: Replace Missing Values with Mean

  val validMarks = data.flatMap(_._2)

  val mean = validMarks.sum / validMarks.length

  val cleanData = data.map {
    case (name, marks, gender) =>
      (name, marks.getOrElse(mean), gender)
  }

  println("Mean: " + mean)
  println("Marks: " + validMarks)
  println("Clean Data: " + cleanData)
}


